"How to use creative tools inside the Khan Kids app – Khan Academy (https://khankids.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/21188738836763-How-to-use-creative-tools-inside-the-Khan-Kids-app)\nciteturn732view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://khankids.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/21188738836763-How-to-use-creative-tools-inside-the-Khan-Kids-app\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 66\nL0: 【0†Skip to main content】\nL1: \nL2: 【1†Submit a request】\nL3: \nL4: [Input][Input] [Input: Search]\nL5: \nL6: Articles in this section\nL7:   * 【2†Our Accessibility Statement】\nL8:   * 【3†Five ways to use Khan Kids for back to school success】\nL9:   * 【4†Quick start guide for preschool through 2nd grade teachers】\nL10:   * 【5†✨ NEW: Teacher Dashboard on the web】\nL11:   * 【6†✨ NEW: Manage student access to areas of the app】\nL12:   * 【7†Module 1: Setting up a Class Account】\nL13:   * 【8†Learning Topics: Using Khan Academy Kids in Educational Settings】\nL14:   * 【9†Module 2: Using Class Codes】\nL15:   * 【10†Daily Schedules for Ages 2-8】\nL16:   * 【11†Module 3: Assigning lessons】\nL17: 【12†See more】\nL18: # How to use creative tools inside the Khan Kids app\nL19: \nL20:   * February 26, 2026 23:45\nL21:   * Updated\nL22: \nL23: Did you know the Khan Academy Kids app has a suite of creative tools to encourage open-ended learning and exploration? Kids can draw, fill in coloring pages, record their voice, make stickers move, and more.\nL24: \nL25: To access these creative tools, go to the Khan Academy Kids library and then select the Create tab 🖍️.\nL26: \nL27: 【13†Image: Home.png】  |    | 【14†Image: CKK 2023 Library Create.png】\nL28: You'll see fun coloring pages featuring animals, vehicles, characters from the Khan Kids app, and more. You'll also see backgrounds that kids can use as a starting point for their creative masterpiece.\nL29: Select a coloring page or background, and then tap the blue pencil in the top right corner to access all the creative tools. Tapping the blue pencil will make two panels appear: one on the right side, with icons for stickers, colored pencils, and crayons; and one on the top, with icons for undoing the last action, recording your voice, and listening to your recording.\nL30: \nL31: 【15†Image: makestory.png】\nL32: You can see these options in the image above. Here's a little bit more detail about what each icon allows you to do:\nL33:   * Bear: When you tap the bear icon on the right side, the bottom of the screen turns into a menu of stickers that kids can drag onto the screen.\nL34:   * Colored pencil: The menu turns into colored pencils to allow for more detailed drawing.\nL35:   * Crayon: The menu goes back to crayons, including a fun rainbow crayon that makes colorful streaks!\nL36:   * Arrow: Press this button to undo your last action.\nL37:   * Microphone: Press this button to record your voice. While recording your voice, you can also move stickers around to make an animated creation. When you're done recording, press the square \"stop\" button.\nL38:   * Play button: Select the play button to watch what you recorded.\nL39: 【16†Image: numberstory.png】  |    | 【17†Image: retellstory.png】\nL40: Kids use the Create tab to make a number story. This is a common mathematics exercise in Kinder-1st grade classrooms. Five cats meet four bats in a spooky forest. How many animals are there altogether? Count all the animals to find out, and pair it with an equation for extra practice.  |    | Kids use the Create tab to retell a story that they just read with their class, or with their parent at home. They use stickers to select the main characters: three pigs and a big, bad wolf.\nL41: Kids record their voice and move the stickers around to tell the story in their own words.\nL42: \nL43: \nL44: Saving and exporting art or artwork\nL45: When kids are done with their artwork or creation, tap the green checkmark in the bottom right corner. Their work will be saved at the very bottom of the Create tab in the Gallery section. You can even help them export their creation to the camera roll to share with family and friends! The GIPHY below will show you how to save your child's art, or you can learn more 【18†here】.\nL46: \nL47: 【19†Image: Gallery_Export_Video_Final.gif】\nL48: \nL49: Was this article helpful?\nL50: [Button: Yes] [Button: No]\nL51: \nL52: 1 out of 1 found this helpful\nL53: \nL54: Have more questions? 【1†Submit a request】\nL55: \nL56: 【20†Return to top】\nL57: ## Comments\nL58: \nL59: 0 comments\nL60: \nL61: Article is closed for comments.\nL62: \nL63: 【21†Khan Academy】\nL64: \nL65: 【22†Powered by Zendesk†www.zendesk.com】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHow do I save artwork from the Gallery? – Khan Academy (https://khankids.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/6477686235419-How-do-I-save-artwork-from-the-Gallery)\nciteturn732view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://khankids.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/6477686235419-How-do-I-save-artwork-from-the-Gallery\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 49\nL0: 【0†Skip to main content】\nL1: \nL2: 【1†Submit a request】\nL3: \nL4: [Input][Input] [Input: Search]\nL5: \nL6: Articles in this section\nL7:   * 【2†Festive winter learning with Khan Academy Kids】\nL8:   * 【3†Meet inspiring women in our new books!】\nL9:   * 【4†Meet a new set of friends in the Khan Kids app!】\nL10:   * 【5†Find books and lessons in the Khan Kids Library】\nL11:   * 【6†How do I save artwork from the Gallery?】\nL12:   * 【7†Sandy's Instruments and Reya's Bugs】\nL13:   * 【8†Podcast Recommendations for Kids】\nL14:   * 【9†Learn more about the characters inside Khan Academy Kids】\nL15:   * 【10†Research from University of Massachusetts Amherst shows Khan Academy Kids boosts pre-literacy skills】\nL16:   * 【11†New first-grade lessons in Khan Academy Kids!】\nL17: 【12†See more】\nL18: # How do I save artwork from the Gallery?\nL19: \nL20:   * February 27, 2026 00:17\nL21:   * Updated\nL22: \nL23: We've added a new feature to Khan Academy Kids. Now, users can export Gallery artwork to their devices to save and share with friends. Here are the steps for capturing that creative energy:\nL24:   1. Go to the Create tab in the app's Library.\nL25:   2. Scroll to the Gallery at the bottom of the Create tab, as shown in the video below.\nL26:   3. Tap the gray \"Enable export\" button in order to activate the export feature.\nL27:   4. Select the artwork you'd like to export by tapping the navy arrow on the image.\nL28:   5. You should now see the artwork in your device's photo storage or camera roll.\nL29: \nL30: 【13†Image: Gallery_Export_Video_Final.gif】\nL31: \nL32: Was this article helpful?\nL33: \nL34: [Button: Yes] [Button: No]\nL35: 0 out of 1 found this helpful\nL36: \nL37: Have more questions? 【1†Submit a request】\nL38: \nL39: 【14†Return to top】\nL40: ## Comments\nL41: \nL42: 0 comments\nL43: \nL44: Article is closed for comments.\nL45: \nL46: 【15†Khan Academy】\nL47: \nL48: 【16†Powered by Zendesk†www.zendesk.com】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFAQ: How do I turn off videos and coloring ? – Khan Academy (https://khankids.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/13849896234395-FAQ-How-do-I-turn-off-videos-and-coloring)\nciteturn732view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://khankids.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/13849896234395-FAQ-How-do-I-turn-off-videos-and-coloring\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 49\nL0: 【0†Skip to main content】\nL1: \nL2: 【1†Submit a request】\nL3: \nL4: [Input][Input] [Input: Search]\nL5: \nL6: Articles in this section\nL7:   * 【2†Our Accessibility Statement】\nL8:   * 【3†Five ways to use Khan Kids for back to school success】\nL9:   * 【4†Quick start guide for preschool through 2nd grade teachers】\nL10:   * 【5†✨ NEW: Teacher Dashboard on the web】\nL11:   * 【6†✨ NEW: Manage student access to areas of the app】\nL12:   * 【7†Module 1: Setting up a Class Account】\nL13:   * 【8†Learning Topics: Using Khan Academy Kids in Educational Settings】\nL14:   * 【9†Module 2: Using Class Codes】\nL15:   * 【10†Daily Schedules for Ages 2-8】\nL16:   * 【11†Module 3: Assigning lessons】\nL17: 【12†See more】\nL18: # FAQ: How do I turn off videos and coloring ?\nL19: \nL20:   * February 26, 2026 23:44\nL21:   * Updated\nL22: \nL23: You can turn off videos and coloring pages from your teacher view. To get to your teacher view, open the app and tap your teacher avatar. Enter your password and you'll see the screen below. Select Settings in the top left corner.\nL24: \nL25: 【13†Image: Teacher_Settings_Arrow.png】\nL26: ​Then, scroll down to the \"Class Preferences\" section. You'll see options to \"Show students Create tab\" and \"Show students Videos tab.\" If you would like to hide these tabs from students, toggle the setting to \"OFF.\"\nL27: \nL28: 【14†Image: ShowStudentsCreate.png】【15†Image: ShowStudentsVideosAndCreate.png】\nL29: \nL30: You can also require students to complete assignments before exploring other areas of the app. That setting is titled \"Show students assignments first.\" You can learn more about it 【16†here】.\nL31: Was this article helpful?\nL32: \nL33: [Button: Yes] [Button: No]\nL34: \nL35: 1 out of 1 found this helpful\nL36: \nL37: Have more questions? 【1†Submit a request】\nL38: \nL39: 【17†Return to top】\nL40: ## Comments\nL41: \nL42: 0 comments\nL43: \nL44: Article is closed for comments.\nL45: \nL46: 【18†Khan Academy】\nL47: \nL48: 【19†Powered by Zendesk†www.zendesk.com】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n✨ NEW: Manage student access to areas of the app – Khan Academy (https://khankids.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/17031195532059--NEW-Manage-student-access-to-areas-of-the-app)\nciteturn732view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://khankids.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/17031195532059--NEW-Manage-student-access-to-areas-of-the-app\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 67\nL0: 【0†Skip to main content】\nL1: \nL2: 【1†Submit a request】\nL3: \nL4: [Input][Input] [Input: Search]\nL5: \nL6: Articles in this section\nL7:   * 【2†Our Accessibility Statement】\nL8:   * 【3†Five ways to use Khan Kids for back to school success】\nL9:   * 【4†Quick start guide for preschool through 2nd grade teachers】\nL10:   * 【5†✨ NEW: Teacher Dashboard on the web】\nL11:   * 【6†✨ NEW: Manage student access to areas of the app】\nL12:   * 【7†Module 1: Setting up a Class Account】\nL13:   * 【8†Learning Topics: Using Khan Academy Kids in Educational Settings】\nL14:   * 【9†Module 2: Using Class Codes】\nL15:   * 【10†Daily Schedules for Ages 2-8】\nL16:   * 【11†Module 3: Assigning lessons】\nL17: 【12†See more】\nL18: # ✨ NEW: Manage student access to areas of the app\nL19: \nL20:   * February 26, 2026 23:46\nL21:   * Updated\nL22: \nL23: We've added new Teacher Settings that allow you to manage student access to areas of the app! Click 【13†here】 to see how to access your Teacher Settings.\nL24: \nL25: \nL26: \nL27: ❤️ Show students Assignments first\nL28: When you toggle this setting \"ON\", students will be required to complete assignments before they can do anything else in the app. After all assignments are complete, the other areas of the app will light up for students to explore.\nL29: \nL30: 【14†Image: Untitled】\nL31: \nL32: \nL33: \nL34: 🖍️ Show students Create tab\nL35: When you toggle this setting \"ON,\" students will not be able to access the Create tab. The Create tab is the tab with the crayon and is only available on the student side of the app. It has coloring pages and backgrounds for kids to draw, write, and record their voice.\nL36: \nL37: \nL38: \nL39: ⏯️ Show students Videos tab\nL40: When you toggle this setting \"ON,\" students will not be able to access the Videos tab. The Create tab is the tab with the teal play button. It includes short videos that introduce academic concepts and a few videos from our friends at Super Simple Songs.\nL41: #### How to access your Teacher Settings\nL42: \nL43:   1. Open the app and tap \"Sign in with Khan Kids account.\" Enter your Khan Kids username and password.\nL44:   2. Tap your teacher avatar. It should display a bear character with your name below.\nL45:   3. Enter your password again and enter your teacher view.\nL46:   4. Look in the top left corner for your Teacher Settings.\nL47: \nL48: 【15†Image: Email3BTS_EmbeddedGIF.gif】\nL49: \nL50: Was this article helpful?\nL51: \nL52: [Button: Yes] [Button: No]\nL53: \nL54: 2 out of 3 found this helpful\nL55: Have more questions? 【1†Submit a request】\nL56: \nL57: 【16†Return to top】\nL58: ## Comments\nL59: \nL60: 0 comments\nL61: \nL62: Article is closed for comments.\nL63: \nL64: 【17†Khan Academy】\nL65: \nL66: 【18†Powered by Zendesk†www.zendesk.com】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFAQ: How do I sign out? – Khan Academy (https://khankids.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/360043669551-FAQ-How-do-I-sign-out)\nciteturn732view4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 6 days ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://khankids.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/360043669551-FAQ-How-do-I-sign-out\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 53\nL0: 【0†Skip to main content】\nL1: \nL2: 【1†Submit a request】\nL3: \nL4: [Input][Input] [Input: Search]\nL5: \nL6: Articles in this section\nL7:   * 【2†Our Accessibility Statement】\nL8:   * 【3†Five ways to use Khan Kids for back to school success】\nL9:   * 【4†Quick start guide for preschool through 2nd grade teachers】\nL10:   * 【5†✨ NEW: Teacher Dashboard on the web】\nL11:   * 【6†✨ NEW: Manage student access to areas of the app】\nL12:   * 【7†Module 1: Setting up a Class Account】\nL13:   * 【8†Learning Topics: Using Khan Academy Kids in Educational Settings】\nL14:   * 【9†Module 2: Using Class Codes】\nL15:   * 【10†Daily Schedules for Ages 2-8】\nL16:   * 【11†Module 3: Assigning lessons】\nL17: 【12†See more】\nL18: # FAQ: How do I sign out?\nL19: \nL20:   * February 26, 2026 23:45\nL21:   * Updated\nL22: \nL23: In Khan Academy Kids, users can choose to create a Parent Account or Class Account.\nL24: \nL25: To sign out from a Parent Account, you will need to navigate to the Parent Section shown below.\nL26: \nL27:   * Open the app and tap For Parents at the bottom of the screen.\nL28:   * Follow the swipe instructions.\nL29:   * Tap the dropdown menu and select Sign Out.​​\nL30: 【13†Image: ParentSection_ForParents.png】  | 【14†Image: ParentSection_Dropdown.png】\nL31: To sign out from a Class Account, go to the User Select screen shown below. Tap Sign Out in the bottom right corner. Note: If you're using a Clever Account, look for the Sign Out link from the main teacher or student view.\nL32: \nL33: 【15†Image: UserSelect_SignOut.png】\nL34: \nL35: Was this article helpful?\nL36: \nL37: [Button: Yes] [Button: No]\nL38: \nL39: 2 out of 2 found this helpful\nL40: \nL41: Have more questions? 【1†Submit a request】\nL42: \nL43: 【16†Return to top】\nL44: ## Comments\nL45: \nL46: 0 comments\nL47: \nL48: Article is closed for comments.\nL49: \nL50: 【17†Khan Academy】\nL51: \nL52: 【18†Powered by Zendesk†www.zendesk.com】\n"
